# Line-ending policy for the Foundation repository.
#
# `instruction-manuals/` holds the DISTRIBUTED copies of the root master
# instruction manuals. They must stay byte-identical to
# `.project/deployment-info/instruction-manuals/` in the root
# governance repository and are verified with SHA-256 (procedure in that
# directory's README). Automatic line-ending conversion would silently break
# that contract on any machine with `core.autocrlf=true`, so the manuals are
# stored and checked out verbatim — no text conversion, ever.
#
# Edit the MASTER and re-propagate; never edit a distributed copy in place.
instruction-manuals/** -text

# Asset artwork is verified BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# `assets/**` is the SOURCE asset tree and `public/assets/**` is its mirrored
# runtime derivative (`scripts/sync-runtime-assets.mjs`, `pnpm assets:check`,
# `tests/unit/asset-taxonomy-mirror.test.ts`). The mirror proof is a SHA-256
# comparison of the two files as they exist on disk, and the favicon contract
# compares the branding mark with the favicon derived from it — so no automatic
# line-ending conversion may rewrite either side. Store source artwork and its
# runtime mirror verbatim.
assets/** -text
public/assets/** -text
